 # Add Chorus participant audience metadata to room messages
 
-
+Chorus room messages should include broker-owned participant/audience metadata so recipients know who is in the room and who will see replies. Current visible custom message includes roomId, postId, from, broker route, and message, but not participant names. Active widget knows selected peers locally, but recipient agents do not reliably get that list in model context. Add broker-injected participants:string[] or audience metadata to room posts/deliveries/custom-message details and model-facing content. Broker should populate it from peer set + local author identity; send/reply tools should not require agents to provide it. Renderer can use details participants; model XML can include concise participants block/attribute.
